## Draft issue 1

Title: gpu-mali: glmark2-es2 buffer columns=200:interleave=false:update-dispersion=0.9:update-fraction=0.5:update-method=map on the NanoPC-T6: oom: yakogl: out of GPU memory for # bytes (# frees held)

Cause 1: oom: yakogl: out of GPU memory for # bytes (# frees held)

The first glmark2-es2 run on the NanoPC-T6 (Mali-G610, panthor, back end gpu-mali, #20) from main `099b5df6` (kernel 6.18.55-current-rockchip64, the tools/mali/panthor-gles pair, libGLESv2.so.2 sha256 `3f6c0a1d9e2b4c5a`), one glmark2-es2 process per scene at 800x600 on an EGL pbuffer, gives verdict oom in 1 scene(s): `[buffer] columns=200:interleave=false:update-dispersion=0.9:update-fraction=0.5:update-method=map`.

- `[buffer] columns=200:interleave=false:update-dispersion=0.9:update-fraction=0.5:update-method=map`: exit 0, timeout 0, panthor kernel lines 0; 4.35 ms a frame
  > yakogl: out of GPU memory for 7684096 bytes (1 frees held)
  > yakogl-mali-exit: draws=2300 refused=0 first_refused=- gpu_faults=0 job_timeouts=0

Run directory `faults`, tallied by `tools/cts/glmark2-mali-tally.py`. Rerun the scene alone with tools/cts/mali-glmark2-run.sh to reproduce. ROADMAP.md stage 2 asks for all 33 scenes with no failed scene, no GL error and no scene out of GPU memory.

